■ JCROSS_FRAG_7c6a95b0
【状態】 確定
【主体】 Warp Weft Yarns In Inkle weaving yarn
【関係】 runs
【客体】 lengthwise on loom is called warp while yarn crosses over under warp is called weft You will need to choose two different colors of yarn for warp weft you want to create stripes patterns

[L2_Archive]
Warp and Weft Yarns: In Inkle weaving, the yarn that runs lengthwise on the loom is called the "warp," while the yarn that crosses over and under the warp is called the "weft." You will need to choose two different colors of yarn for the warp and the weft if you want to create stripes or patterns.

